{
  "answer": "Your olive top and burgundy skirt do not clash; they work well together with good contrast near your face. However, you lack a third piece to style the look properly, and bare arms are exposed which is risky for autumn weather.",
  "verdict": "wear_with_change",
  "works": [
    {
      "about": "colors_together",
      "items": ["p1", "p1-2"],
      "text": "The muted olive green of your top sits next to the deep burgundy skirt without competing; they have a solid contrast in value, so your face is highlighted by the lighter green."
    },
    {
      "about": "palette",
      "items": ["p1"],
      "text": "Your top is an edge-of-palette shade that feels interesting next to the base neutral of the skirt, creating a modern mix."
    },
    {
      "about": "silhouette",
      "items": ["p1", "p1-2"],
      "text": "The straight cut of the top and the simple skirt shape make for an easy, relaxed silhouette that does not overwhelm your frame."
    }
  ],
  "change": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "items": ["p1"],
      "text": "Wearing a cardigan or blouse instead of this top would give you a third layer to tie the outfit together and protect your arms from the cold."
    },
    {
      "id": "f-o1-1",
      "items": ["p1", "p1-2"],
      "text": "Adding a cardigan or blouse will also fix the lack of a styled third piece, making the look more complete and ready for cooler weather."
    }
  ]
}
